# LaunchDek Compliance

Gate before presenting final code. If any checklist item is "no", fix it first.

See `launchdek-project.mdc` (architecture), `launchdek-standards.mdc` (quality), `wordpress-php.mdc` (PHP/REST patterns).

## Security

- Sanitize on input, escape on output, authorize before action.
- REST: every route has `permission_callback`; use `LAUNCHDEK_Capabilities::current_user_can()`.
- Admin UI auth: `X-WP-Nonce` with `wp_rest` nonce on all `fetch` calls.
- Never expose decrypted Application Passwords in REST responses, logs, or audit entries.
- Store credentials via `LAUNCHDEK_Credential_Vault::encrypt()`; decrypt only at request time in `LAUNCHDEK_Remote_Client`.
- Settings API: `sanitize_callback`, `show_in_rest => false`.
- Remote requests: validate URLs with `esc_url_raw()`; use `wp_remote_*` with timeouts; handle `WP_Error`.
- SQL: `$wpdb->prepare()` only; no user input in table names.
- Webhook URLs: sanitize with `esc_url_raw()`; only POST on configured user events.

## Remote Site Access

- Core automation model: WordPress core REST API + Application Passwords for API checklist steps, connection tests, and drift reads.
- Optional client checklist panel: hub auto-deploys the bundled mu-plugin to `wp-content/mu-plugins/` when a site is saved or tested with credentials, on initial checklist push, or via manual **Refresh Client Panel** — user-initiated via site registration or run push, not undisclosed. Panel files are whitelisted bundle copies only; install route validates paths and requires hub Application Password auth. Routine step toggles and hub `sync_run()` do not reinstall the bundle (`push_run( $id, false, false )`).
- Connection tests must not leak credentials in error messages shown to non-privileged users.
- Payload mapper must whitelist/validate endpoint paths and methods before remote execution. Mutating `/wp/v2/settings` payloads must pass through `LAUNCHDEK_Payload_Mapper::filter_excluded_payload()` so hub `exclude_options` strip sensitive fields before remote execution; audit `api_step_executed` may include `excluded_fields` when fields were stripped.
- Checklist `deep_link` values are wp-admin paths — store via `LAUNCHDEK_Admin_Deep_Links::normalize_stored_path()`, not `esc_url_raw()` (which strips bare paths like `options-general.php`). Full URLs are built at display/push time via `LAUNCHDEK_Remote_Client::admin_link()` or client `admin_url()`.
- Drift verification reads remote state for comparison only — no arbitrary code execution.
- Client run callbacks use per-run `client_run_token` (`hash_equals` in `can_client_token_access_run`; `ensure_client_token()` backfills legacy runs) — never expose tokens in hub REST responses, logs, or audit entries shown to non-privileged users; token travels only in hub→client run snapshots and client→hub callback headers.
- Client step notes require non-empty text; save locally on the remote site first, then sync to hub. Hub note storage uses `filter_step_notes()` to drop empty/duplicate entries. Optional screenshot attachments are gated by per-step `show_screenshot_field` (requires `show_note_field`); use existing remote media library attachment IDs only (`wp.media` on the client site) — not arbitrary file uploads to the hub.
- Client panel **Dismiss** clears the local completed-run snapshot on the remote site only; it does not delete hub run records.
- Auto-capture is user-initiated (`can_edit_checklists` on hub, logged-in client admin on remote); records only whitelisted admin actions (REST settings mutations, plugin activate/deactivate) into ephemeral client option data — not background telemetry.
- Legacy audit actions (`workflow_created`, `workflow_updated`) and webhook `details.workflow` are read-only backward-compat shims — new code must use `checklist_*` keys and `details.checklist`.

## Directory & Privacy

- No obfuscated code or undisclosed telemetry.
- Outbound requests are limited to: user-registered remote sites (including mu-plugin deploy/push), user-configured webhook URLs, and integration adapters (user-initiated push).
- Integrations **Telemetry Sync Mapping Rules** store field-mapping preferences only (`telemetry_sync_rules`); they do not emit tracking data.
- Webhook and integration behavior must be documented in `readme.txt`.
- No spammy readme or deceptive behavior.

## Code Quality

- Prefer WordPress core APIs over custom hacks.
- Keep code human-readable for directory review.
- Follow WPCS across PHP, CSS, JS, and HTML.
- Enqueue assets via `is_plugin_screen()` only.
- Use `launchdek` / `LAUNCHDEK_` prefix consistently.

## Self-Review Checklist

- [ ] No WordPress core modifications
- [ ] GPL-compatible
- [ ] Human-readable, reviewable code
- [ ] User-facing strings translatable (`LAUNCHDEK_TEXT_DOMAIN`)
- [ ] REST routes: capability checks on every endpoint
- [ ] Credentials encrypted at rest when enabled; never leaked in API responses
- [ ] Input sanitized; output escaped
- [ ] SQL prepared in repositories
- [ ] Remote calls use timeouts and error handling
- [ ] Webhooks opt-in and user-configured
- [ ] Uninstall drops all tables, options, and capabilities
- [ ] Unique `LAUNCHDEK_` / `launchdek_` prefix
- [ ] Would survive WordPress.org review

## Unsafe Requests

If a feature conflicts with the Plugin Handbook, Coding Standards, security best practices, privacy expectations, or Directory Guidelines — refuse the unsafe approach and propose a compliant alternative.
